{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_kIiAoaUlH8bzrkiunevg7Guc","content":"1\t(ns yin.repl\n2\t  \"The local Yin shell for DaoStream: explicit state, synchronous steps.\n3\t\n4\t   This namespace owns no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock, or namespace\n5\t   global.  It holds the one shell value a driver threads: the evaluator beside\n6\t   its separately-owned program media — `program-in`, which the macro\n7\t   expander observes, and `program-out`, which the evaluator's own observer\n8\t   watches (`docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md` §10.1) — the language, the value\n9\t   history, the output medium with its cursor, and a per-medium ledger\n10\t   recording the last outcome that medium answered.  Every function takes a\n11\t   state and returns the next one.\"\n12\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [] :jolt [[jolt.scheme :as scheme]] :default [])\n13\t            #?(:cljd [clojure.edn :as edn]\n14\t               :cljs [cljs.reader :as reader])\n15\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n16\t            [dao.pretty :as pretty]\n17\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n18\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n19\t            [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n20\t            [yin.repl.ast-index :as ast-index]\n21\t            [yin.repl.dht :as repl.dht]\n22\t            [yin.repl.index :as index]\n23\t            [yin.repl.query :as query]\n24\t            [yin.repl.store :as store]\n25\t            [yin.repl.state :as config]\n26\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n27\t            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as ast-walker]\n28\t            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n29\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n30\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n31\t            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n32\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as register]\n33\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as stack]\n34\t            [yin.vm.encoder :as encoder]\n35\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n36\t            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n37\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n38\t            [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n39\t            [yin.vm.macro :as macro]\n40\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n41\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n42\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n43\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]))\n44\t\n45\t\n46\t(def output-capacity\n47\t  \"Declared capacity of the composition-owned output medium, in elements.\"\n48\t  4096)\n49\t\n50\t\n51\t(def ingress-capacity\n52\t  \"Declared capacity of the composition-owned program medium, in elements.  The\n53\t   shell is the only appender and its one step owner serializes evaluation, so\n54\t   eviction can only follow a producer the composition does not make; a gap is\n55\t   therefore fatal to the current evaluation rather than a normal operating\n56\t   condition.\"\n57\t  4096)\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(def drain-budget\n61\t  \"Maximum elements one output drain reads.  It equals the output capacity,\n62\t   so one drain reaches every element the medium still holds, the round's\n63\t   result included.\"\n64\t  output-capacity)\n65\t\n66\t\n67\t(def gap-budget\n68\t  \"Maximum `gap` answers one output drain accepts.  A gap is not an element,\n69\t   so it is counted apart from `drain-budget`: a gap never costs the drain\n70\t   an element, and the drain stays total against a transport that could"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_zkz3IXDCsg1y90qBQIfRCOvm","content":"1\t(ns yin.repl.frontends\n2\t  \"The REPL's standard frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section\n3\t   8.5.6, slice F2): the hand-written Clojure frontend and the ANTLR PHP and\n4\t   Python frontends installed into a `yang.frontend` catalog. This is\n5\t   the only place the REPL composition names a language's namespace;\n6\t   `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the catalog selects.\n7\t\n8\t   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with\n9\t   `:input :forms` when the frontend consumes the forms the shell reader\n10\t   already read, else the source text.\"\n11\t  (:require\n12\t    [yang.clojure :as yang.clojure]\n13\t    [yang.frontend :as frontend]\n14\t    [yang.php :as yang.php]\n15\t    #?@(:cljd [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n16\t               [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n17\t               [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]]\n18\t        :default [[yang.python.antlr.repl :as python.antlr.repl]\n19\t                  [yang.python.antlr.parser :as python.antlr.parser]\n20\t                  [yang.python.antlr.repl-probe :as python.antlr.probe]])\n21\t    [yin.repl :as repl]))\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t(defn- manifest\n25\t  [id language]\n26\t  {:yang.frontend/id id,\n27\t   :yang.frontend/spi 1,\n28\t   :yang.frontend/revision \"legacy-1\",\n29\t   :yang.frontend/language language,\n30\t   :yang.frontend/grammar {:yang.grammar/package \"none\",\n31\t                           :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"program\"},\n32\t                           :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1},\n33\t   :yang.frontend/options-schema :segment/none,\n34\t   :yang.frontend/lowering-profile :segment/legacy,\n35\t   :yang.frontend/runtime-profile :segment/legacy,\n36\t   :yang.frontend/support-profile :segment/legacy})\n37\t\n38\t\n39\t(defn- clojure-lower\n40\t  [forms]\n41\t  (if (= 1 (count forms))\n42\t    (yang.clojure/compile (first forms))\n43\t    (yang.clojure/compile-program forms)))\n44\t\n45\t\n46\t(defn- antlr-manifest\n47\t  []\n48\t  (assoc (manifest :yang/python :python)\n49\t         :yang.frontend/revision \"f4\"\n50\t         :yang.frontend/grammar\n51\t         {:yang.grammar/package \"python3\",\n52\t          :yang.grammar/entries {:module \"file_input\"},\n53\t          :yang.grammar/export-profile :yang.cst/v1,\n54\t          :yang.grammar/targets #{:java :javascript :dart}}))\n55\t\n56\t\n57\t(defn standard\n58\t  \"The standard catalog. The Clojure frontend consumes the forms the\n59\t   shell's own reader read, so its parse stage is the identity.  The ANTLR\n60\t   frontend is the Python frontend, installed on every host, each running\n61\t   its own generated target of the one grammar.  It shows what a submission\n62\t   printed and the value rendered by its `:render` (Python repr).\"\n63\t  []\n64\t  (cond-> frontend/empty-catalog\n65\t    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang/clojure :clojure)\n66\t                           {:input :forms,\n67\t                            :parse identity,\n68\t                            :lower clojure-lower})\n69\t    true (frontend/install (manifest :yang/php :php)\n70\t                           {:parse identity, :lower yang.php/compile})\n71\t    #?@(:cljd [true (frontend/install\n72\t                      (antlr-manifest)\n73\t                      {:parse (fn [source]\n74\t                                (python.antlr.parser/parse-source (str source \"\\n\"))),\n75\t                       :lower python.antlr.repl/lower,\n76\t                       :primitives python.antlr.repl/primitives,\n77\t                       :lower-session python.antlr.repl/lower-session,\n78\t                       :render python.antlr.repl/display-value,\n79\t                       :probe python.antlr.probe/probe})]\n80\t        ;; jolt (J5): installed over the C++ parser when native/jolt-parser"}
