{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_fb0he4XqeGndQCsSDJh6y0hu","content":"1\t(ns yang.antlr.packet\n2\t  \"The target-neutral parse-tree IR and its reader (docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n3\t   §5.5). ANTLR has no neutral tree: each target materializes its own\n4\t   parse-tree objects. This namespace owns the neutral form every host's\n5\t   exporter produces (`yang.antlr.cst`, one file per host) and every\n6\t   language's CST-to-UAST converter consumes: the CST packet, version 1.\n7\t\n8\t   Packet (version 1):\n9\t\n10\t     {:yang.cst/version 1\n11\t      :yang.cst/unit u\n12\t      :yang.cst/grammar id\n13\t      :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/ok | :yang.cst/syntax-error | :yang.cst/source-error\n14\t      :yang.cst/root 0                       ; ok only\n15\t      :yang.cst/nodes [record ...]           ; ok only, preorder, id = index\n16\t      :yang.cst/errors [error ...]           ; non-ok only\n17\t      :yang.cst/complete true}\n18\t\n19\t   Rule record  {:id n :kind :rule :rule \\\"name\\\" :children [ids] :span [s e]}\n20\t   Token record {:id n :kind :token :type \\\"NAME\\\" :text t :span [s e]}\n21\t                 plus :synthetic true when the token's text is not the source\n22\t                 at its span (indentation helpers, EOF); its span is then\n23\t                 zero-width.\n24\t   Error record {:kind :syntax-error :message m :line l :column c :span [s e]}\n25\t\n26\t   Spans are half-open UTF-8 byte offsets into the sealed source. A unit with\n27\t   any syntax error yields an error packet and no nodes: never a partial\n28\t   program.\n29\t\n30\t   Invariants every target's exporter must meet (`validate!` checks 1, 6 and\n31\t   7 structurally, and 2-5 against the source when it is given; `conform` is\n32\t   the source-aware check as a vector of violations):\n33\t\n34\t     1. ids are preorder indexes; :root is 0; child edges form a tree\n35\t        (`validate!`).\n36\t     2. :rule is the grammar rule name from the parser's rule-name table,\n37\t        never a target class name; :type is the symbolic token name, else the\n38\t        literal name, else the decimal type, \\\"EOF\\\" for EOF.\n39\t     3. :span is half-open UTF-8 byte offsets into the sealed source. Each\n40\t        target converts its own index unit at the boundary (the JVM indexes\n41\t        code points; the JS and Dart streams are opened in code-point mode).\n42\t     4. A token is :synthetic with a zero-width span and the canonical helper\n43\t        text of its type exactly when `synthetic-policy` says so: DEDENT and\n44\t        EOF always, NEWLINE only at the end of the source, no other type ever.\n45\t        A real token's text is the source at its span.\n46\t     5. A rule's span covers its real children only; an empty rule is\n47\t        zero-width.\n48\t     6. Any syntax error yields an error packet with :yang.cst/errors and no\n49\t        nodes.\n50\t     7. :yang.cst/grammar names the grammar revision and tool; the target does\n51\t        not appear in the packet. Target equivalence is the contract.\n52\t\n53\t   Portable and language-agnostic: child edges are data, so the tree is\n54\t   validated before anything walks it.\"\n55\t  (:require\n56\t    [dao.host.text :as text]))\n57\t\n58\t\n59\t(def packet-version 1)\n60\t\n61\t\n62\t;; =============================================================================\n63\t;; Source text\n64\t;; =============================================================================\n65\t\n66\t(defn code-points\n67\t  \"The code points of `s` as a vector of integers (`dao.host.text`: a\n68\t   surrogate pair is one code point, an unpaired surrogate its own).\"\n69\t  [s]\n70\t  (text/code-points s))\n71\t\n72\t\n73\t(defn utf8-length\n74\t  \"The UTF-8 byte count of one code point.\"\n75\t  [cp]\n76\t  (cond (< cp 0x80) 1\n77\t        (< cp 0x800) 2\n78\t        (< cp 0x10000) 3\n79\t        :else 4))\n80\t\n81\t\n82\t(defn utf8-bytes\n83\t  \"The UTF-8 byte count of a string: span ends are checked against it.\"\n84\t  [s]\n85\t  (reduce + 0 (map utf8-length (code-points s))))\n86\t\n87\t\n88\t(defn byte-offsets\n89\t  \"Byte offset of each code point index of `cps`, plus the total at index n.\"\n90\t  [cps]\n91\t  (loop [out [0]\n92\t         acc 0\n93\t         cps (seq cps)]\n94\t    (if cps\n95\t      (let [acc (+ acc (utf8-length (first cps)))]\n96\t        (recur (conj out acc) acc (next cps)))\n97\t      out)))\n98\t\n99\t\n100\t(def synthetic-policy"}
