{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_UZuV780Y9gUlXKYgnKKtrmy7","content":"1\t(ns host-boundary.closure\n2\t  \"The adopted closure of dao.stream.host-boundary.md §3.1, per lane.\n3\t\n4\t   A require-form traversal from yin.repl.main over the ns declarations,\n5\t   parsed by clojure.tools.namespace.parse (read-ns-decl with the lane's\n6\t   reader features, deps-from-ns-decl for :require, :use and\n7\t   :require-macros; :as-alias and string (npm, dart:) libspecs are not\n8\t   dependencies). Lane features: :clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs},\n9\t   :cljd #{:cljd :clj} (the cljd build also reads :clj arms; the first\n10\t   matching arm wins, as in tools.reader). A namespace resolves to\n11\t   src/<lane>/<path>.<lane> first (the shadow: yin.repl.host is\n12\t   host.cljc on the JVM, host.cljs and host.cljd elsewhere), then\n13\t   src/cljc/<path>.cljc; a namespace with neither (clojure.core, a\n14\t   library) is outside the closure.\n15\t\n16\t   It is not a compiler-resolved call graph: it over-includes a namespace\n17\t   required but unused, and does not see dynamic loading.\n18\t\n19\t   Each file is tagged with its §3.1 classes (a set: a file can sit in\n20\t   several rows of the §3.1 table; :none means no host contact beyond the\n21\t   §3.3 exempt syntax).\n22\t\n23\t   Run from the repo root:\n24\t     clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:hb {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"]\n25\t                      :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace\n26\t                                   {:mvn/version \\\"1.5.0\\\"}}}}}' \\\\\n27\t       -M:hb -m host-boundary.closure [--check]\n28\t   writes docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn and\n29\t   prints the totals; --check writes nothing and exits 1 when a committed\n30\t   file differs from the computed closure."}
